 "narrative": [
  "To complete a major, students are required to take fourteen courses, comprising four courses in the introductory sequence (2A, 2B, 100A, 100B), and ten upper-division courses.",
  "Critical gender studies will accept up to two upper-division courses as overlap requirements for the two majors [double major].",
  "Directed Group Study (198), Independent Study (199), internships can be taken only with a P/NP grade option; the number of such courses to be applied to the major should be carefully discussed with a critical gender studies adviser.",
  "The page does not state the degree type; BA assumed."
